ops.body:
The root reposync history-cache patch (reviews/reposync-history-cache.patch, base 826a351, only worktree/history.go +16/−6 and history_test.go +89) applies cleanly (`git apply --check`) on cc-sync/worktree-snapshot @ 826a351.
- Merge: the reposync fix-group Run wf_37624322-e25 (triage running) has root-history marked ROOT-OWNED, and its merge stage reads the epic for the patch location, so it now applies this patch in the final merge.
- Targeted refutation: a separate Run wf_54499b1e-30a applies the patch in a scratch worktree at 826a351 (no commit, removed after), re-runs both reproductions and the focused tests (-race -count=3), and tries to break it with real-git variants:
  - a missing middle bundle;
  - a GC'd chain tip still in the ledger;
  - an amend/rebase after partial chain loss;
  - sha256 object format;
  - concurrent capture over a shared common dir;
  - transient git errors, which must surface rather than silently rebuild;
  - plus a source read-only check.
- Also landed: the synckit final-fix 803da5d (11 distinct issues from 17 findings, all reproduced and fixed, PR #4 CI green). Targeted refutation + the harness/WaitIdle merge + the CommitBatch re-measure are running (Run wf_619de18b-756).
